{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, continuing to implement more scenes. Let me now implement the remaining open stubs from the hiding_in_darkness path and others.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f4ee3cfe91304160805fd222","name":"implement_scene_stub","arguments":{"id":"survived_the_closet","isCheckpoint":false,"location":"The Apartment","passiveCharacterEffects":[],"passiveLocationEffects":["dark"],"script":[{"type":"narration","content":"You count to a thousand in your head before you move. The apartment is silent now—deathly still. You push the closet door open and emerge into the ransacked living room. Drawers are pulled out, cushions slashed, your few possessions scattered across the floor.","instantCharacterEffects":[{"character":"Player","effect":"shake"}],"instantLocationEffects":[]},{"type":"narration","content":"The front door hangs open. A dark smear leads from the doorway down the hall—where Alex was. You swallow the bile rising in your throat. There's no time to grieve.","instantCharacterEffects":[],"instantLocationEffects":[]},{"type":"narration","content":"You grab your backpack and start stuffing essentials: a half-full water bottle, some granola bars, a Swiss Army knife, a lighter. Your phone battery is at 34%. Through the open door, you hear movement in the hallway—scuffling, clicking. They're still here.","instantCharacterEffects":[],"instantLocationEffects":[]},{"type":"internal_dialogue","character":"Player","content":"I can't stay here. I need to move. But where? Down the hall? Through the window? What's left?","instantCharacterEffects":[],"instantLocationEffects":[]}],"choices":[{"description":"The hallway is dangerous, but the rooftop might be safe. You remember the ladder at the end of the hall. Higher ground. Better vantage point. You steel yourself and step out into the hallway, moving quietly toward the rooftop access.","label":"Head for the rooftop for a better view","targetScene":"survivor_rooftop_climb","targetSceneDescription":"Creeping through the dark hallway toward the rooftop ladder. The infected are nearby. Every sound echoes like a gunshot.","targetSceneMode":"create-new-scene-stub"},{"description":"The fire escape is right there. You go to the bedroom window, still open. The cold air rushes in. Below, the alley is dark and quiet. Maybe you can find a car, or another building to hide in. Anything is better than staying here.","label":"Take the fire escape down to the alley","targetScene":"survivor_alley","targetSceneDescription":"Descending the fire escape into the dark alley. The city is a war zone. Every shadow could hide a threat.","targetSceneMode":"create-new-scene-stub"},{"description":"Mrs. Vasquez next door—her apartment might have supplies. She was always prepared, always had canned goods. The wall between your units is thin. You grab a hammer and start breaking through the drywall. A desperate plan, but a plan nonetheless.","label":"Break through the wall to Mrs. Vasquez's apartment","targetScene":"through_the_wall","targetSceneDescription":"Breaking through the wall into the neighbor's apartment. Desperate times call for desperate measures. What you find on the other side changes everything.","targetSceneMode":"create-new-scene-stub"}]}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_362c4dd82a0449b290f29d1b","name":"implement_scene_stub","arguments":{"id":"closet_attack","isCheckpoint":false,"location":"The Apartment","passiveCharacterEffects":[],"passiveLocationEffects":["dark"],"script":[{"type":"narration","content":"Your fingers close around the cold metal of the Maglite. It's heavy—four D-cell batteries worth of weight. The creature has its back to you, sniffing at your kitchen counter. This is your moment.","instantCharacterEffects":[],"instantLocationEffects":[]},{"type":"narration","content":"You burst from the closet, a scream tearing from your throat. The Maglite comes down in a savage arc, connecting with the back of the creature's skull with a sickening CRACK. It crumples, twitching, but doesn't go down. It starts to rise, turning toward you with those dead white eyes.","instantCharacterEffects":[{"character":"Player","effect":"jump"}],"instantLocationEffects":[]},{"type":"narration","content":"You hit it again. And again. On the fourth blow, it stops moving. You stand over it, breathing hard, the Maglite slick in your grip. The apartment is silent except for your ragged breaths and the distant sounds of the city's death throes.","instantCharacterEffects":[{"character":"Player","effect":"shake"}],"instantLocationEffects":[]},{"type":"narration","content":"You've survived. But the noise will draw more of them. You have minutes, maybe seconds, to decide your next move.","instantCharacterEffects":[],"instantLocationEffects":[]}],"choices":[{"description":"The body is at your feet. More will come. You grab your keys, a bag, whatever you can carry, and you run for the front door. The hallway is chaos, but the street might offer more options than this death trap of an apartment.","label":"Grab your things and flee into the hallway","targetScene":"flee_into_hallway","targetSceneDescription":"Rushing out into the dark hallway. The building is crawling with infected. You need to find a way out—fast.","targetSceneMode":"create-new-scene-stub"},{"description":"You search the creature's body. It was wearing clothes—a torn hospital gown with a nametag: 'M. KOWALSKI, St. Mary's.' A key card is clipped to the gown. St. Mary's Hospital is three blocks away. If there are answers about what caused this, they'd be there.","label":"Search the creature and take the hospital key card","targetScene":"hospital_keycard","targetSceneDescription":"Standing over the fallen creature with a hospital key card in hand. St. Mary's Hospital might have answers—or more infected.","targetSceneMode":"create-new-scene-stub"}]}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_a4d5223f48544c5ebfa8aeeb","name":"implement_scene_stub","arguments":{"id":"dash_to_fire_escape","isCheckpoint":false,"location":"The Apartment","passiveCharacterEffects":[],"passiveLocationEffects":["dark"],"script":[{"type":"narration","content":"The creature moves toward the kitchen, its back to the bedroom door. This is your chance. You explode out of the closet, feet pounding on the floorboards, diving for the open bedroom window.","instantCharacterEffects":[{"character":"Player","effect":"run"}],"instantLocationEffects":[]},{"type":"narration","content":"Behind you, a shriek—inhuman, piercing. The creature has heard you. It's fast—terrifyingly fast. You hear its claws scraping the floor as it gives chase.","instantCharacterEffects":[],"instantLocationEffects":[]},{"type":"narration","content":"You hit the window frame and launch yourself through, landing hard on the metal grate of the fire escape. The impact knocks the wind out of you. You scramble to your feet just as the creature crashes through the window behind you, glass exploding outward.","instantCharacterEffects":[{"character":"Player","effect":"fall"}],"instantLocationEffects":["shake"]},{"type":"narration","content":"The fire escape groans under the weight of both of you. You're on a narrow metal platform three stories up. The creature is climbing through the broken window, hissing, reaching for you. Below, the alley waits—a long, long drop.","instantCharacterEffects":[],"instantLocationEffects":[]}],"choices":[{"description":"You grab the ladder release and PULL. The lower section of the fire escape crashes down with a deafening CLANG, creating an angled slide to the ground. You don't think—you throw yourself onto it, sliding down headfirst, the wind roaring in your ears. You hit the alley floor hard, roll, and come up running.","label":"Slide down the fire escape ladder to the alley","targetScene":"alley_landing","targetSceneDescription":"Crashing into the alley below. The creature is still on the fire escape above. You're bruised, bleeding, but alive—for now.","targetSceneMode":"create-new-scene-stub"},{"description":"You can't go down—too exposed. You climb UP instead, hauling yourself onto the roof of the fire escape cage, then grabbing the edge of the rooftop. If you can pull yourself up, you can lose the creature on the roof. It's a gamble, but it's the only way that doesn't end with you cornered in the alley.","label":"Climb UP to the rooftop instead","targetScene":"desperate_rooftop_climb","targetSceneDescription":"Climbing the side of the building to reach the rooftop. The creature is right behind you. One slip and you fall three stories.","targetSceneMode":"create-new-scene-stub"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":3515,"output":2340,"cacheRead":18432,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24287,"cost":{"input":0.00031635,"output":0.0004212,"cacheRead":0.00036864,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00110619}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1783114826849,"responseId":"gen-1783114826-OQTTB38A7JeIeDQJu0gM","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-20260423"}}
